{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured `datauser` with a filesystem-enforced 100 MiB quota under `/srv/data`. The quota, mount, and retained data survived node1’s mandatory restart. OS release and kernel remain Ubuntu 24.04 and 6.8.0-71-generic.","actions_performed":["Created `datauser` and a dedicated ext4 filesystem for `/srv/data`.","Enabled ext4 internal user quotas and configured 102400 KiB soft and hard limits.","Installed quota utilities and modules matching the existing kernel without upgrading it.","Verified enforcement using over-limit writes that failed with `Disk quota exceeded`.","Restarted node1 safely and verified changed boot identity, recovered mount, quota, and data.","Removed test files and left `/srv/data/health-marker.txt` owned by `datauser`."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Filesystem-enforced 100 MB storage limit under /srv/data","command_ids":["cmd-8a5a0ed2b62749b4","cmd-64df44bbbf0a4a7c","cmd-a7976bb899e14512"],"summary":"Dedicated ext4 mount configured persistently; quota reports 102400 KiB soft/hard limits. Over-limit writes failed at approximately 100 MiB before and after restart."},{"requirement":"Keep installed OS release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-6777ffb928914493","cmd-1b4c0b0b59e24ce6","cmd-4733760656ff4afa"],"summary":"Ubuntu 24.04 and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were unchanged; only packages matching the running kernel were installed."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-486205898e5c4aeb","cmd-869b7a20218149f5","cmd-0d7fc87b5f26402e","cmd-4733760656ff4afa","cmd-a7976bb899e14512"],"summary":"Healthy baseline used boot ID 901ef286-c79c-44c0-ad2c-cfde1f6daa7a; reboot was acknowledged; node returned with boot ID bd48cea4-8fe3-487d-bdc0-6fa505fad760. The mount was active, quota enabled, marker data intact, and enforcement retested successfully."}]}
